  "packId": "tide_pool",
  "_comment": "What the storm left on the reef, and what lives there. Arabic labels carry full harakat: diacritics are not optional for ages 3-8, and the benefit of vowelisation is strongest in exactly this band.",
  "_buoyancyComment": "`buoyancy` is the attribute the float/sink round sorts on, and the cast is cross-balanced against `size` in BOTH directions on purpose. Driftwood, a coconut and a crate are big and float; a key and a coin are tiny and sink. A child whose rule is 'big things sink' is wrong on the second piece, and a child whose rule is 'small things float' is wrong on the third. Neither hypothesis survives long enough to feel confirmed, which is the whole point of the round.",
  "_weightComment": "`weight` lives HERE rather than in the activity so a stone weighs three in every story it turns up in. A thing that is heavy in one chapter and light in the next is not a world, it is a quiz.",
